= ui_card "Card Helper"
  p.sp-text-muted <code>ui_card(title = nil, **options, &block)</code>

  h3 Philosophy
  p Cards are the fundamental containers in Slim-Pickins. They group related information and actions, providing a "paper-like" surface hierarchy.
  ul
    li <strong>Encapsulation:</strong> Keeps content visually distinct from the background.
    li <strong>Structure:</strong> Enforces a standard header/body layout (optional header).
    li <strong>Modularity:</strong> Easily nestable and composable.

  h3 Arguments
  = ui_table ["Name", "Type", "Description"],
    [["title", "String (Optional)", "If provided, renders a header section with this title."],
     ["options", "Hash", sp_safe("Standard HTML attributes (e.g., <code>class</code>, <code>id</code>).")],
     ["block", "Block", "The content to render inside the card body."]]

  h3 Real World Scenarios

  h4 1. Standard Content Container
  p The most common use case: wrapping a section of content.

  .sp-card
    .sp-card__body
      = ui_card "Project Alpha" do
        p Status: Active
        p Due: Tomorrow

      = ui_code do
        | = ui_card "Project Alpha" do
            p Status: Active
            p Due: Tomorrow

  h4 2. Headless Card
  p Use a card without a title for simple grouping.

  .sp-card
    .sp-card__body
      = ui_card do
        p Just some grouped text without a header.

      = ui_code do
        | = ui_card do
            p Just some grouped text without a header.
